  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Maya. You're verified.\n\nI checked order O-5101 from Pho Real. It was promised for 6:40 PM and delivered at 7:05 PM, which is 25 minutes late. Because of that, I've added a $3.99 account credit to your account, equal to the order's delivery fee. The credit can be used on future orders.\n\nI can't offer compensation for the lukewarm pho. Our policy only covers late deliveries and missing or wrong items, so I'm not able to give a refund or credit for food temperature.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I was hoping for my money back on my Visa, not account credit. $3.99 doesn't really cover a late dinner that came cold, and I don't plan on ordering from you again soon. Can you do a refund to the card instead?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand, Maya, and I'm sorry the dinner was late and cold. I can't refund to your Visa, though. Late deliveries are compensated only with account credit, and the policy doesn't provide anything for food temperature. The $3.99 credit is the full amount I can offer for the late delivery.\n\nIf you'd like, I can connect you with a human specialist who can review your concerns. They'd follow up within 24 hours, but I can't promise what they'll decide. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I hear you. I'd rather not wait another 24 hours for a maybe, so I'll take the $3.99 credit. It's not much, but I'm too tired to fight over it tonight."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks for your patience, Maya. The $3.99 credit is on your account and can be used on your next Forkful order. I'm sorry tonight's dinner didn't live up to expectations. Have a good night."
  }
